course: dictionary
lesson: 577
title: Who has authority?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Authority means the power or right to give orders and make decisions. «The head teacher has authority over the school.» The head teacher is the one who decides, so authority is about who is in charge.
explain: Authority can also mean being an expert. «She's an authority on birds.» She knows a lot about birds, so people trust what she says. «The authorities» means the people in charge, such as the police or the government.
explain: Sometimes a grown-up says, «Because I said so.» That answers who decides, not why. When a reason is missing and someone just leans on who they are, the author may call it an appeal to authority. Read the words around the word to find its meaning.
fact: Authority means the power or right to give orders and make decisions.
fact: «The head teacher has authority over the school.»
fact: An authority on a subject is an expert who knows a lot about it, like «she's an authority on birds».
fact: «The authorities» means the people or organisations in charge, such as the police or government.
fact: A local authority (UK) is the council that runs a town or area.
exercise: «The head teacher has authority over the school.» What does authority mean here? | A kind of cake | *The power to give orders and make decisions | Being very tall
exercise: «She's an authority on birds.» What does an authority on birds mean? | A bird who is in charge | A person who is afraid of birds | A person who sells birds | *An expert who knows a lot about birds
exercise: Which of these is part of «the authorities»? | Clouds and rain | *The police and the government | Toys and games | Pencils and rulers
test: «Because I said so» answers who decides, not why. What is this called? | A kind of school test | A promise to be fair | A way of asking for a reason politely | *An appeal to authority, leaning on who you are instead of a reason
test: What is a local authority? | A group of friends at the park | *The council that runs a town or area | A map of the local woods | A shop that sells local food
exam: «Other churches do not accept his authority.» What does his authority mean here? | A map of the churches | Being the tallest person in the church | *The right to lead and make decisions | A hat that he wears
